            {
              "text": "Depending on whether you mean **Newcastle upon Tyne (UK)** or **Newcastle, NSW (Australia)**, several consultancies specialize in Microsoft Copilot Studio, custom AI agents, and practical Power Platform workflow automation for mid-market businesses. \n\n---\n\n### If you are in **Newcastle upon Tyne (UK & North East)**\n\n#### 1. **Marra** *(Newcastle upon Tyne)*\n* **Focus:** Microsoft Copilot Studio & Custom Copilot Agent Development.\n* **Why they fit:** Based directly in Newcastle, Marra specifically specializes in turning \"AI ambition into adoption\" using Copilot Studio. They run Discovery & Design workshops to identify high-impact mid-market use cases and build custom AI agents integrated with Microsoft 365, Power Automate, and existing ERP/CRM databases.\n* **Core strengths:** Low-code agent orchestration, multi-channel deployment (Teams, web portals), and operational workflow automation.\n\n#### 2. **Cybit** *(Newcastle upon Tyne / North Tyneside)*\n* **Focus:** Microsoft Solutions Partner (Cloud, Data, Security & AI).\n* **Why they fit:** Headquartered near Newcastle, Cybit is one of the premier mid-market IT and cloud consultancies in the North East. They help mid-sized businesses implement Microsoft 365 Copilot and build specialized autonomous or semi-autonomous AI agents via Copilot Studio to eliminate repetitive administrative tasks.\n* **Core strengths:** Tenant readiness, Azure AI / Copilot data security, Power Platform connector builds, and end-to-end managed workflows.\n\n#### 3. **SR1 Development** *(Newcastle upon Tyne)*\n* **Focus:** Practical Power Platform & Microsoft 365 Process Digitization.\n* **Why they fit:** A hands-on, boutique team of Microsoft developers and consultants who excel at pragmatic workflow modernization. If your mid-market business is transitioning from manual spreadsheets, approvals, and legacy databases, SR1 connects Power Apps, Power Automate, and Copilot tools to create streamlined automated flows.\n* **Core strengths:** Straightforward, non-hyped process automation (e.g., invoice approvals, request triage, intake workflows).\n\n#### 4. **AI Vision Consulting** *(Newcastle upon Tyne)*\n* **Focus:** Practical AI Automation & Capability Building.\n* **Why they fit:** A Newcastle-based consultancy focusing specifically on helping businesses make practical use of the AI capabilities already within their Microsoft stack (Copilot, internal search agents, automated document summarisation) rather than over-engineering complex architectures.\n\n#### 5. **Version 1** *(Newcastle Delivery Hub)*\n* **Focus:** Enterprise & Mid-Market Microsoft Business Applications.\n* **Why they fit:** If your mid-market organization has complex enterprise systems (e.g., Dynamics 365, complex ERPs), Version 1’s major Newcastle branch has dedicated Power Platform and Agentic AI solution architects who design multi-step Copilot Studio agents that tie directly into core operations.\n\n---\n\n### If you are in **Newcastle, NSW (Australia)**\n\n* **Nettko *(Newcastle, NSW)*:** Strongly focused on safe, compliance-first AI automation for mid-market and regulated businesses. They audit SharePoint and Dataverse permissions before deploying Microsoft Copilot and build targeted intake, classification, and workflow pipelines using the Microsoft ecosystem.\n* **Frontrow Technology *(servicing Newcastle / Hunter Valley)*:** Specializes in Copilot Studio architecture, Microsoft AI readiness, and agent governance.\n\n---\n\n### What to Ask When Evaluating a Mid-Market Copilot Consultant\n\nWhen building agents with Copilot Studio, mid-market businesses typically struggle with data security and ROI. Ensure the partner you select evaluates the following:\n\n1. **Permission & Data Governance First:** Copilot Studio agents inherit your internal data access models. A good consultant will audit your SharePoint and Dataverse permissions first so the agent doesn't expose sensitive payroll or executive documents.\n2. **Connector Strategy (Action over Chat):** Ensure they design agents that execute actions via **Power Automate** and custom APIs (e.g., updating an ERP, creating an approval, fetching a vendor record), rather than just deploying a glorified knowledge-base FAQ bot.\n3. **Licensing & Message-Pack Optimization:** Microsoft Copilot Studio uses a consumption/session model. Your consultant should demonstrate how they optimize prompts and actions to prevent unexpected tenant billing spikes.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
